      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As a coordinator, I approach these minor disruptions with the same methodical focus I apply to flight schedules, treating them as low-level, predictable obstacles that require a structured workaround. When these persistent, small annoyances crop up, the key is to compartmentalize them, perhaps by implementing a \"triage\" system—a quick, decisive action to neutralize the distraction before it escalates into a full-blown logistical nightmare. I find that dedicating a specific, short block of time *before* deep work to \"clearing the desk\" of these minor irritations prevents them from bleeding into the critical planning phase. This allows you to maintain the high-level strategic view of the Singapore-Bangkok-HCMC transit without the constant, nagging interference.",
      "source": "target",
